<center><h2>About Me</h2></center>
<center><p>Welcome to my site; I'm <strong>Panzerschokolade</strong>.</p>

<p>I’m a Software Engineering student from Australia. Since childhood, I’ve been fascinated by computers, as well as politics and history—particularly stories of war, sovereignty, and nationalism. This site is my attempt to preserve relics from a world that is often forgotten, sanitized, or erased as time moves forward.</p>

<p>The bunker I’ve built is a tribute to war aesthetics, political dissent, and the internet’s lost art of free thought. It’s more than just a collection of media—it’s a personal archive, a journey through forgotten corners of history and the digital landscape.</p>

<p>The <strong>Schokolade Net Bunker</strong> aims to preserve content from a time before censorship and sanitization became the norm. The material here is uncensored, politically incorrect, and often controversial—because truth isn’t always comfortable, and it shouldn’t come with a filter.</p>

<p>This project started as a personal outlet for my interests in IT, war aesthetics, and political history, while exploring the last wild frontiers of the internet. My goal is to eventually expand it into a comprehensive archive and network.</p>
